# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# CampusConnect mobile — copy this file to `.env` and edit the one value below.
#
#   cp .env.example .env
#
# EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL is the ONLY place the backend address is configured. It is
# read once, in src/lib/api.ts. Nothing else in the app hardcodes a host.
#
# The `EXPO_PUBLIC_` prefix is mandatory — Expo only inlines variables with that
# prefix into the client bundle. A variable named API_URL would silently be
# undefined on the phone.
#
# WHY NOT localhost: the app runs on your PHONE. `localhost` there means the
# phone itself, not your dev machine, so it must be the dev machine's LAN IP.
# The phone and the dev machine have to be on the SAME Wi-Fi network.
#
# HOW TO FIND YOUR LAN IP:
#   Windows  →  ipconfig            (look for "IPv4 Address" under your Wi-Fi
#                                    adapter, e.g. 192.168.29.217)
#   macOS    →  ipconfig getifaddr en0
#   Linux    →  hostname -I
#
# This value CHANGES when you join a different Wi-Fi network (or when your
# router hands out a new lease). If the app shows "Cannot reach the
# CampusConnect API", re-run the command above and update this line.
#
# After editing, restart Metro so the new value is baked into the bundle:
#   npx expo start --clear
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

EXPO_PUBLIC_API_URL=http://192.168.29.217:5000
